Title = {Novel P-N-Si synergistic phase-change material microcapsules for
   building coatings with smart temperature control and fire safety
   functions},
Journal = {APPLIED THERMAL ENGINEERING},
Year = {2026},
Volume = {288},
Number = {1},
Month = {MAR},
Abstract = {In order to save building energy consumption and improve the comfort of
   building occupancy, functional building coatings are widely used.
   Introducing microencapsulated phase change materials into epoxy resin
   coatings can endow them with temperature-control properties. To enhance
   the fire safety of buildings, this study, for the first time, couples
   P-N-Si three-element synergistic flame retardancy with phase-change
   thermal control. Hexachlorocyclotriphosphazene (HCCP) and silane
   coupling agent (3-Aminopropyl)triethoxysilane (APTES) was used as raw
   materials to prepare a new type of P-N-Si synergistic flame retardant
   (APZ) through nucleophilic substitution reaction. The introduction of
   APZ endows epoxy resin (APZ-PCM/EP) with excellent flame-retardant
   properties, and the peak heat release rate and total smoke production of
   APZ-PCM/EP are reduced by 22.9 \% and 27.3 \% respectively. Furthermore,
   the thermal responsiveness and phase change properties of the
   microcapsules modified with APZ (APZ-PCM) are enhanced, with the onset
   temperature of phase change occurring 1.5 degrees C earlier than that of
   MPCM. More importantly, the indoor temperature in the small-scale model
   room using APZ-PCM/EP is reduced by 29.5 \% compared to that of the pure
   epoxy resin. This study presents a viable route to integrate fire safety
   with thermal comfort and offers a new strategy for smart
   temperature-control intumescent coatings on building exterior walls.},
